// Title: Network Communication Initiated To Portmap.IO Domain
// Sigma ID: 07837ab9-60e1-481f-a74d-c31fb496a94c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-05-31 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: T1041, command-and-control, T1090.002, exfiltration
// Description: Detects an executable accessing the portmap.io domain, which could be a sign of forbidden C2
//   traffic or data exfiltration by malicious actors
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of portmap.io domains
// References:
//   - https://portmap.io/
//   - https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/issues/11337
//   - https://pro.twitter.com/JaromirHorejsi/status/1795001037746761892/photo/2
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_domain_portmap.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where RemoteUrl endswith ".portmap.io"
